Subject: [PATCH 05/54] =?UTF-8?q?ngram-bias:=20GPU=20backend=20sampler=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20steering=20+=20backend-sampling=20compatibles?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Transforme le sampler ngram_bias (steering logits[token] += alpha*ln(p)) en
llama_sampler_backend complet, sur le modele du sampler logit_bias:

- extrait common_ngram_cache_lookup_bias() (stupid backoff -> paires token/bias)
- backend_apply: data->logits += ggml_set_rows(zeros, ngram_bias, ngram_idxs)
- backend_set_input: lookup CPU -> tensor_set de 512 paires max (padding no-op)
- le bias n-gram s'applique sur GPU AVANT le top-k GPU -> top-k reste backend

Resultat mesure (bench_xhigh 6 questions): steering alpha=0.2 + backend-sampling
= 30.45 t/s vs 30.64 baseline sans steering (-0.6%), au lieu de retomber a 24.9
(-16%) avec l'ancien sampler CPU. Fini le conflit vitesse/qualite.
